      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dc821f2e-bbc4-5831-ab02-6581184fbbca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenneth Arnold, Raymond A. Palmer\n- Events: World UFO Day, 1947 Roswell UFO Incident, Kenneth Arnold UFO sighting\n- Places: Mount Rainier, Washington, United States\n- Products: The Coming of the Saucers, Mystic, Search, Flying Saucers\n- Concepts: unidentified flying objects, flying saucers\n\nFacts:\n- On June 24, 1947, Kenneth Arnold claimed to see nine unusual objects flying in tandem near Mount Rainier, Washington, in what is generally considered the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States.\n- July 2 is observed by World UFO Day to commemorate the supposed UFO crash in the 1947 Roswell UFO Incident.\n- June 24 is observed by World UFO Day because it marks Kenneth Arnold’s widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States.\n- Raymond A. Palmer published magazines including Mystic, Search, and Flying Saucers.\n- Raymond A. Palmer co-wrote the flying saucer book The Coming of the Saucers with Kenneth Arnold.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
